JOKE DOOR, written on the 8-9/10/93 by Ari Tsironis.

OK firstly you run this prog as a door, ie function 34!

KEY  FUNCTION  EXTRA  LOW  HIGH   PATH/FILENAMES
 J      34       0    10   10000  DOORS:Joke/Joke DOORS:Joke/jokes.config

With the PATH/FILENAMES the "DOORS:Joke/jokes.config" tells the door
where the config file is, you need the full path, etc!  MAXS is pretty
brain dead here, so you might not have enough room!  If so, then just
rename everything to smaller names!

eg  PATH/FILENAMES
    DOORS:J/Joke DOORS:J/jokes.config


OK You need to have a DOORS: assign setup!  You then need to make a
directory in there to hold everything, this can be any name, but you might
have to shorten it, for the above reason!

So do this....
             assign DOORS: in your user-startup
         
             makedir DOORS:joke


Then you need to have four files.
 
	1: The joke door, which is called joke
	2: A jokes.config file
	3: A jokes_title.text file
	4: A jokes_list.text file


1:  This is the door I wrote, just copy it into your new directory!

2:  This file allows the setting up of everything!
    eg  It has 6 options, which must be in the following order!
            a: PATH/FILENAME of the title screen
            b: PATH/FILENAME of the jokes list
            c: View Jokes List, Key, MUST BE UPPERCASE
            d: Add to Jokes List, Key, MUST BE UPPERCASE
            e: Download Jokes List, Key, MUST BE UPPERCASE
            f: Exit Jokes Key, MUST BE UPPERCASE

    The example one I have done for ya is:
           
            doors:j/jokes_title.text 
            doors:j/jokes_list.text 
            V 
            A 
            D 
            X

3:  This file is an ANSI of the menu/screen you want to appear, when the
user selects this door!  I've done a real simple bodgey one, please make a
better/nicer one!  

4:  This is the list of jokes, ie the jokes file.


That's about it!  Hope ya like it, and that it works properly for ya!
As I said I won't be available for a few days, so please leave me some
mail, if ya have any probs/queries/suggestions etc!


Ari...